slide layout=cover align=center valign=middle justify=#false {
  title "Look and feel"
  text "Alignment, themes, backgrounds, motion and deck.json."
  text "Every slide here uses what it describes · press **→**"
  notes #"""
    Theming and layout: part of the slides manual. Source: examples/theming.
    """#
}

slide {
  heading "What's inside"
  list numbered {
    - "Alignment and spacing"
    - "Themes, backgrounds and classes"
    - "Motion: transitions and speed"
    - "Header, footer and deck-wide defaults"
    - "deck.json, fonts and CSS"
  }
  notes #"""
    Press o at any time for the slide drawer, h for help. Every slide in this deck is live: it uses the feature it describes.
    """#
}

slide {
  heading "Slide settings"
  text "The properties of a `slide` node. Every one applies to that slide only."
  code "text" {
    frame #"""
      slide layout=cover          cover (a title slide, no header/footer, big heading)
            theme=light           built-in or custom theme name
            background="bg.jpg"   image path/URL or any CSS value
            align=center          left | center | right (default left)
            valign=middle         top | middle | bottom (default top)
            justify=#true         justified paragraphs
            class=spotlight       extra CSS class on the stage
            title="Short title"   shown in the presenter view
            transition=slide      fade | slide | slide-right | slide-left | zoom | none
            animate=#true         continue the previous slide
            footer=off            hide the deck's footer/header on this slide
            --accent="#ff9e64"    any CSS variable
      """#
  }
  notes #"""
    The next slides demonstrate theme, background, class, valign and transitions.
    """#
}

slide justify=#true align=left valign=top {
  heading "Alignment: everything starts at the top left"
  text "Every box starts at the **start**, both ways: text at the left edge, at the top. Say otherwise with `align` (`left`, `center`, `right`) and `valign` (`top`, `middle`, `bottom`). They work on a `slide`, on a `row`, a `col` or a text node, in `defaults` of the `deck`, and on a `code`."
  text "`justify=#true` stretches every line of a paragraph to the full column width, like in a printed document; the last line stays at the start. This slide uses it. `defaults justify=#true` in the `deck` switches it on for a whole deck."
  text "The built-in layouts choose their own alignment: `cover`, `quote` and `center` center everything, the column layouts center their columns vertically. This slide has none of these: it starts at the top left, and says so with `align=left valign=top`."
  notes #"""
    start and end are accepted too: start = left/top, end = right/bottom.
    """#
}

slide align=right {
  heading "align=right"
  text "The heading, the text and the media all sit on the right edge."
  list {
    - "lists follow"
    - "and quotes"
    - "and images"
  }
  image "diagram.svg" alt=diagram height="70px"
}

slide align=center valign=middle {
  heading "align=center valign=middle"
  text "The whole block is centered, both ways. Good for a title, a quote or a closing slide."
  notes #"""
    Only this slide: the deck default stays start/start.
    """#
}

slide valign=bottom {
  heading "valign=bottom"
  text "The text sits at the bottom of the slide, above the footer."
}

slide --heading-size="72px" --text-size="28px" --item-gap="26px" --stage-padding="8vmin 12vmin" --accent="#ffb454" {
  heading "Sizes and spacing"
  text "CSS variables as properties of the slide: the knobs of the theme, for this slide only:"
  list {
    - "`--heading-size` and `--text-size`: any CSS length"
    - "`--item-gap`: the gap between text blocks"
    - "`--stage-padding`: the slide's inner margin"
    - "`--accent`, `--heading`, `--fg`: colors for this slide"
  }
  notes #"""
    Any CSS length works: 4vmin, 2rem, 30px. Deck-wide values go in `vars` of the deck.
    """#
}

slide {
  row {
    col size="34%" {
      heading "Column widths: `size`"
      text "In a `row` every part takes an equal share of the width. `size=34%` makes this one narrower, here for a short note next to wider code. `size=2` would be a weight: twice as wide."
    }
    code "typescript" {
      frame #"""
        const columns = { text: "34%", code: "the rest" };
        """#
      frame #"""
        const columns = { text: "34%", code: "the rest", gap: "4vmin" };
        """#
    }
  }
}

slide theme=midnight layout=cover background="bg.svg" {
  title "`cover`"
  text "Large centered heading, ideal with a background image."
  notes #"""
    background accepts an image path (relative to the .slides file) or any CSS background value.
    """#
}

slide theme=paper background="linear-gradient(160deg, #f4ecd8, #e8d9b5)" {
  heading "Per-slide theme and background"
  text "`theme=paper` and a CSS gradient background, for this slide only. The next slide goes back to the deck theme; the change crossfades."
  notes #"""
    Themes are sets of CSS variables, so a theme switch also recolors the code tokens.
    """#
}

slide theme=sunset {
  heading "A custom theme: `sunset`"
  text "Defined once under `themes` in this deck's `deck.json` and used here with `theme: sunset`. It also joins the **t** key cycle."
  code "typescript" id=g1 align=left {
    frame #"""
      const theme = {
        name: "sunset",
        warm: true,
      };
      """#
    frame #"""
      const theme = {
        name: "sunset",
        warm: true,
        accent: "#ff9e64",
      };
      """#
  }
}

slide theme=terminal {
  heading "A custom theme: `terminal`"
  text "Green on black, with token colors to match. Change a theme and the code tokens recolor, because they are just CSS variables."
  code "bash" id=g1 {
    frame #"""
      $ slides dev my-talk/
        ready in 312 ms
      """#
    frame #"""
      $ slides build my-talk/ -t single
        wrote my-talk.html (3.8 MB)
      """#
  }
}

slide theme=light {
  heading "Built-in `light`"
  text "Crisp on projectors. Per-slide, so you can mix themes inside one deck."
  code "python" id=g1 {
    frame #"""
      def total(prices, tax=0.2):
          return sum(prices) * (1 + tax)
      """#
    frame #"""
      def total(prices, tax=0.2):
          net = sum(prices)
          return round(net * (1 + tax), 2)
      """#
  }
}

slide background="#2d1b4e" theme=midnight {
  heading "Backgrounds: solid colors"
  text "`background: #2d1b4e` — any CSS color. Backgrounds crossfade between slides."
  notes #"""
    Next: radial gradient, stripes, an SVG, and an animated feel via crossfades.
    """#
}

slide theme=midnight background="radial-gradient(circle at 20% 15%, #7a3a5f, #3b1d5c 50%, #120a24 90%)" {
  heading "Backgrounds: gradients"
  text "`background: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 15%, #7a3a5f, #3b1d5c 50%, #120a24 90%)`"
  code "typescript" id=g1 {
    frame #"""
      const sky = "gradient";
      """#
    frame #"""
      const sky = "gradient";
      const sunset = sky + " of warm colors";
      """#
  }
}

slide theme=midnight background="repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, #14142b 0 24px, #191936 24px 48px)" {
  heading "Backgrounds: patterns"
  text "Any CSS works, including `repeating-linear-gradient(...)`. Or point `background=` at an image file, as the cover slides of these decks do with `bg.svg`."
}

slide class=spotlight valign=middle {
  heading "class: spotlight"
  text "This slide adds the CSS class `spotlight`, defined in the deck's own `deck.css` (loaded by `css \"deck.css\"` in the `deck` node)."
  text "`valign=middle` centers this slide's content vertically."
  notes #"""
    deck.css can restyle anything: .stage.spotlight .item h2 { ... }
    """#
}

slide transition=slide {
  heading "Text transitions"
  text "`transition=` sets how a slide's text enters: `fade` (default), `slide`, `slide-right`, `slide-left`, `zoom`, `none`. `animation stagger=` in the deck delays each block after the previous one."
  text "This slide: `slide`."
  notes #"""
    Defaults for the whole deck: `animation transition=… stagger=…` in the deck node.
    """#
}

slide transition=zoom {
  heading "zoom"
  text "Each block scales up while it fades in."
  list {
    - "first"
    - "second"
    - "third"
  }
}

slide transition=slide-left {
  heading "slide-left"
  text "The content travels to the left: the new slide comes in from the right, the old one leaves to the left. `slide-right` is the mirror image, and it moves the code along with the text."
}

slide transition=none {
  heading "none"
  text "No entrance animation for the text: it appears instantly. Code still animates."
  code "typescript" id=g1 {
    frame #"""
      const instant = true;
      """#
    frame #"""
      const instant = true;
      const code = "still animates";
      """#
  }
}

slide --move-dur="1.6s" --fade-dur="0.9s" {
  heading "Slow motion"
  text "Every animation knob is a CSS variable, so a slide can override it: `--move-dur=\"1.6s\"` and `--fade-dur=\"0.9s\"` on the `slide`."
  code "typescript" id=g1 {
    frame #"""
      function area(w: number, h: number) {
        const result = w * h;
        return result;
      }
      """#
    frame #"""
      function area(h: number, w: number) {
        return h * w;
      }
      """#
    frame #"""
      const area = (h: number, w: number) => h * w;
      """#
  }
  notes #"""
    Perfect for a slide where the transition IS the point.
    """#
}

slide --move-dur="0s" --fade-dur="0s" {
  heading "Instant"
  text "`--move-dur: 0s` and `--fade-dur: 0s`: frames switch with no animation at all. (Visitors who ask the OS for reduced motion get this automatically.)"
  code "typescript" id=g1 {
    frame #"""
      const mode = "instant";
      """#
    frame #"""
      const mode = "instant";
      const delay = 0;
      """#
  }
}

slide --move-dur="0.8s" --ease="cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1)" {
  heading "Bouncy"
  text "`--ease: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1)` overshoots a little before settling."
  code "typescript" id=g1 {
    frame #"""
      function greet(name: string) {
        return "Hello, " + name;
      }
      """#
    frame #"""
      function greet(name: string, punctuation = "!") {
        const message = "Hello, " + name + punctuation;
        return message;
      }
      """#
    frame #"""
      const greet = (name: string, p = "!") =>
        `Hello, ${name}${p}`;
      """#
  }
}

slide {
  heading "Themes"
  text "Built in: `dark`, `light`, `paper`. Press **t** to cycle, or open `?theme=light`. Your own theme is a set of CSS variables in `deck.json` and joins the cycle:"
  code "jsonc" {
    frame #"""
      "theme": "ocean",
      "themes": {
        "ocean": {
          "--bg": "#0b1d2a", "--fg": "#b8d4e3", "--heading": "#fff", "--accent": "#3ddc97",
          "--tok-keyword": "#ff7eb6", "--tok-ident": "#e6f4fb", "--tok-type": "#ffd479"
        }
      }
      """#
  }
  notes #"""
    Token colors: --tok-keyword --tok-ident --tok-property --tok-type --tok-builtin --tok-comment --tok-punct --tok-plain. See this deck's own deck.json for two full themes (sunset, terminal).
    """#
}

slide --tok-keyword="#ff5d8f" --tok-ident="#ffe66d" --tok-type="#4ecdc4" --tok-builtin="#ff9f1c" --tok-punct="#8d99ae" --accent="#4ecdc4" {
  heading "Recolor syntax per slide"
  text "This `slide` sets `--tok-keyword`, `--tok-ident`, `--tok-type`, `--tok-builtin` and `--tok-punct` as properties. No theme needed."
  code "typescript" id=g1 {
    frame #"""
      interface Point { x: number; y: number }

      function norm(p: Point): number {
        return Math.sqrt(p.x ** 2 + p.y ** 2);
      }
      """#
    frame #"""
      interface Point { x: number; y: number }

      function norm({ x, y }: Point): number {
        return Math.hypot(x, y);
      }
      """#
  }
}

slide --font-heading="Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif" --heading-size="64px" --text-size="26px" --accent="#e07a5f" {
  heading "A different voice"
  text "`--font-heading`, `--heading-size` and `--text-size` change typography for one slide."
  text "Serif headings and bigger body text, straight from the slide's properties."
  notes #"""
    Deck-wide defaults go in `vars` of the deck.
    """#
}

slide {
  heading "Header, footer and logo"
  text "The bar at the bottom of this very slide is the deck's **footer**. Define a `header` and/or a `footer` in the `deck` node: each has a `left`, `center` and `right` slot holding text or an image (a list of both in `deck.json`)."
  code "text" {
    frame #"""
      deck {
        footer left="logo.svg" right="{slide} / {slides}" height=42 border=#true background="#0b1d2a" color="#9db4c0"
      }
      """#
  }
  text "Text can use `{slide}` `{slides}` `{title}` `{slideTitle}` `{author}` `{date}`. A slot value that ends in `.svg` `.png` `.jpg` `.webp` is an image, relative to the deck folder. Bars are hidden on `cover` slides unless you set `cover=#true`; any slide can opt out with `footer=off` or `header=off`."
  notes #"""
    Typical use: a school or company theme. Put the logo in the footer or header, add the name and the slide number.
    """#
}

slide footer=off {
  heading "This slide has no footer"
  text "`footer=off` on the `slide` hides the bar for one slide, for example in front of a full-screen demo. The bar fades out and the built-in slide counter comes back. The space stays reserved, so nothing on the slide moves when a bar appears or disappears."
  notes #"""
    Same for header=off.
    """#
}

slide {
  heading "Deck-wide defaults"
  text "`defaults` in the `deck` node gives properties to **every** slide. A slide's own properties win."
  code "text" {
    frame #"""
      deck {
        defaults justify=#true margin="9vmin 12vmin" align=left
        vars --heading-size="56px"
      }
      """#
  }
  text "Together with `themes`, `vars`, `header`/`footer` and `css` it is enough to build a house style once and reuse it for every deck of a school or company."
  notes #"""
    Defaults take align, valign, background, margin, justify and transition.
    """#
}

slide {
  heading "deck.json"
  text "Optional, next to the slides. Everything in it can also be written in a `deck` node of a `.slides` file; where both say something, the `deck` node wins."
  code "jsonc" {
    frame #"""
      {
        "title": "My talk",
        "theme": "dark",
        "css": "deck.css",
        "vars": { "--font-heading": "Georgia, serif", "--text-size": "28px" },
        "themes": { "...": {} },
        "fonts": [{ "family": "Fira Code", "src": "fira.woff2", "weight": "400" }],
        "googleFonts": ["Inter:wght@400;700"],
        "animation": { "move": 0.5, "fade": 0.3, "moveDelay": 0.05, "fadeInDelay": 0.1,
                       "ease": "ease-in-out", "slideFade": 0.4,
                       "textTransition": "slide", "textStagger": 0.1 }
      }
      """#
  }
  notes #"""
    Also supported here: "author", "date", "order", "hidden" and "thumbnail", used by the deck gallery.
    """#
}

slide {
  heading "Animation knobs"
  text "Under `animation` in the deck (seconds; in `deck.json` also `moveDelay`, `fadeInDelay`, `slideFade`, `textDrift`):"
  list {
    - "`move` — how long tokens glide to a new position"
    - "`fade` — fade in / out of tokens"
    - "`moveDelay` — moved tokens wait for the fade-out to finish"
    - "`fadeInDelay` — new tokens wait for the move to finish"
    - "`ease` — any CSS timing function"
    - "`slideFade` — background and text crossfade between slides"
    - "`textDrift` — pixels the text drifts while it fades (default 8; `0` for a pure fade); `textStagger` — delay between a slide's blocks (default 0.06)"
  }
  text "Users who prefer reduced motion get instant transitions automatically."
  notes #"""
    Try move: 1.2 for a slow-motion demo.
    """#
}

slide {
  heading "Fonts, variables and CSS"
  list {
    - "`vars` — CSS variables for the whole deck (`vars --text-size=\"28px\"`): `--font-text`, `--font-heading`, `--font-code`, `--text-size`, `--heading-size`, `--move-dur`"
    - "`fonts` — local font files (path relative to the deck folder)"
    - "`googleFonts` — families loaded from Google Fonts"
    - "`css` — a stylesheet for anything else; combine with `class=` on a `slide`"
  }
  text "Code is drawn in the monospace font `--font-code` (Iosevka by default); the layout measures it, so use monospace fonts."
}

slide theme=midnight layout=cover align=center valign=middle justify=#false background="bg.svg" transition=zoom {
  title "That's all"
  text "More decks in this series: **Showcase**, **Writing slides**, **Code animation**, **Presenting and shipping**."
  text "Start your own: `slides new my-talk`"
  notes #"""
    The end.
    """#
}
